# Environment Variables for Downlodr macOS Build and Code Signing
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your Apple Developer credentials

# ==============================================================================
# Apple Developer Code Signing Configuration
# ==============================================================================

# Your Apple Developer ID Application certificate name
# Find this in Keychain Access under "My Certificates"
# Example: "Developer ID Application: Your Name (TEAM123456)"
APPLE_IDENTITY="Developer ID Application: Your Name (TEAM123456)"

# Optional: Separate installer certificate (if you have one)
# This is different from the application certificate and used for PKG installers
# APPLE_INSTALLER_IDENTITY="Developer ID Installer: Your Name (TEAM123456)"

# ==============================================================================
# Apple Notarization Configuration
# ==============================================================================

# Your Apple ID email (used for App Store Connect)
APPLE_ID="your-apple-id@example.com"

# App-specific password for notarization
# Generate this at https://appleid.apple.com/account/manage → App-Specific Passwords
# Create a new password specifically for this app's notarization
APPLE_APP_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD="abcd-efgh-ijkl-mnop"

# Your Apple Developer Team ID
# Find this at https://developer.apple.com/account/#/membership
# Example: "TEAM123456"
APPLE_TEAM_ID="TEAM123456"

# ==============================================================================
# Build Configuration (Optional)
# ==============================================================================

# Set to 'production' for release builds, 'development' for testing
NODE_ENV="production"

# Skip code signing entirely (for development builds)
# Set to 'true' to skip signing even if certificates are available
# SKIP_CODE_SIGNING="false"

# ==============================================================================
# Security Notes
# ==============================================================================
# 
# IMPORTANT SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS:
# 
# 1. Never commit this .env file to version control
# 2. Keep your app-specific password secure and regenerate it if compromised
# 3. Only use these credentials on trusted build machines
# 4. Consider using CI/CD environment variables for automated builds
# 
# ==============================================================================
# Setup Instructions
# ==============================================================================
# 
# To set up code signing and notarization:
# 
# 1. Join the Apple Developer Program ($99/year)
# 2. Generate certificates in Apple Developer Console:
#    - Developer ID Application (for code signing)
#    - Developer ID Installer (optional, for PKG installers)
# 3. Download and install certificates in Keychain Access
# 4. Generate an app-specific password for notarization
# 5. Copy this file to .env and fill in your credentials
# 6. Run: ./scripts/build-macos.sh
# 
# ==============================================================================
# Troubleshooting
# ==============================================================================
# 
# Common issues and solutions:
# 
# Certificate not found:
# - Verify certificate is installed in Keychain Access
# - Check certificate name matches exactly
# - Ensure certificate is not expired
# 
# Notarization failed:
# - Verify Apple ID and app-specific password
# - Check team ID is correct
# - Ensure code signing was successful first
# 
# Build failed:
# - Check that yt-dlp binary is present and executable
# - Verify all dependencies are installed (yarn install)
# - Check build logs for specific error messages
# 
# ==============================================================================
